+------------------------------------------------------+
|            STRESS SAFETY SUPERVISOR BLOCK           |
|              (FOR ANY DC LOAD DRIVER)               |
+------------------------------------------------------+

  SUPPLY & SENSE
  --------------
  [BAT+]----[FUSE]----+------------------+------------------+
                      |                  |                  |
                     [RSENSE]           [NTC]              LOAD
                      |                  |                  |
                     NODE_I            NODE_T              GND

  CURRENT LIMIT (OVER-CURRENT / SHORT)
  ------------------------------------
  NODE_I --> [U1] Comparator (discrete or IC)
              - IN+ = NODE_I (via scale resistors)
              - IN- = I_LIMIT_REF (set by divider)

  U1 OUT --> [Q1] NPN --> pulls GATE_DRIVE low when over-current

  VOLTAGE MONITOR (UNDER-VOLTAGE)
  -------------------------------
  [BAT+] --> divider --> NODE_V

  NODE_V --> [U2] Comparator
              - IN+ = NODE_V
              - IN- = V_MIN_REF

  U2 OUT --> inhibits ENABLE line when battery too low


  TEMPERATURE CUT-OFF
  -------------------
  NODE_T (from NTC) --> [U3] Comparator
                         - IN+ = T_REF
                         - IN- = NODE_T

  U3 OUT --> [Q2] NPN --> latches FAULT when over-temp


  FAULT LATCH & LOGIC
  -------------------
  U1_OUT (I_FAULT)
  U2_OUT (V_FAULT)
  U3_OUT (T_FAULT)

  These go into a simple OR network:

    I_FAULT ----\
                 +----> FAULT_LINE ----[Q3] NPN
    V_FAULT ----/                         |
    T_FAULT ----\                         +--> DISABLE_DRIVE
                 +----> LED_FAULT (via R)

  DISABLE_DRIVE then:
    - pulls MOSFET gate low
    - ignores button input
    - can require manual reset (toggle RESET switch)


  USER INPUT (GENERIC)
  --------------------
  [BTN] --> debounced --> ENABLE_REQ

  ENABLE_REQ AND NOT(FAULT_LINE) --> GATE_DRIVE


+------------------------------------------------------+
| BEHAVIOR                                             |
| - If current > limit → FAULT, drive off              |
| - If battery < min → FAULT, drive off                |
| - If temp > threshold → FAULT, drive off             |
| - FAULT lights LED and can latch until reset         |
+------------------------------------------------------+
